Spec: Loopback two-observation STUN fixture

Purpose:
  Drive actual source-built XTCP discovery and UDP business transport without accessing public endpoints.

Owns:
  ./stun.go

Must:
  Listen only on two owned IPv4 loopback UDP sockets, accept bounded standard Binding requests, echo the exact transaction and return observed source plus the alternate owned endpoint.
  Bound packets and lifetime, close owned sockets on stop and never claim loopback observations classify physical NAT or prove mobile connectivity.

  Export both owned public port numbers so Agent discovery can explicitly authorize two destinations without following an unconfigured alternate.
